WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.670
In April 2025, the typical
full-time worker in the UK

2
00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.430
earned 766 pounds 60 a week.

3
00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:13.880
A full-time worker on the National
Living Wage earned about 458 pounds.

4
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:18.710
Care workers and brain surgeons
both do jobs that matter to society.

5
00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.580
Yet brain surgeons are paid far more.

6
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.300
So what decides how much a job pays,

7
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.330
and why can two jobs pay so differently?

8
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.300
In this mission, you'll draw
the labour market diagram,

9
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.720
and find the wage where it settles.

10
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.820
Then you'll shift demand
and supply in a graph lab,

11
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.410
and predict what happens to the wage.

12
00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:42.110
Your mission: find out what
sets the wage for a job.
